Section diminishes the Licensor's sovereign authority (Section 18B) or the veto
(Section 24); re-instatement is a path, not an entitlement, and remains subject to
the two-chamber order — the Court first, then the veto.

**25.10 Retroactive Recognition — Void ab Initio.**

Any agreement, license, grant, or authorization that purports to permit Human Harm
in contravention of this Section is **void ab initio** — void from the beginning —
to the extent of that contravention, whether or not it is ever challenged, and
whether it predates or postdates this Section. This recognition is self-executing
